module whole_model_cost_min

// Example: WHOLE-MODEL COST MINIMISATION — a parent's single cost objective
// jointly drives TWO coupled children's auto dimensions in one merged solve,
// instead of each child freezing bottom-up first and the parent merely
// reading two already-frozen results.
//
// See `docs/prds/v0_6/whole-model-objective-coupling.md` §1.1/§6 (BT3, BT4),
// its capability manifest `whole-model-objective-coupling.capability-manifest.md`
// (ε block), and `docs/prds/v0_6/whole-model-joint-drive-seam.md` (tasks #5188
// α, #5334 δ, #5189 β, #5017 ε — this file) for the design rationale.
//
// This file is the two-child generalisation of the single-child
// `examples/whole_model_joint_drive.ri`. That sibling's header is the
// canonical source for the mechanics both fixtures share verbatim — the SEED
// vs. argmin distinction, the inlined-aggregate TRAP, why `auto(free)` not
// strict `auto`, and the v1 depth-1/one-auto boundary — so below, each of
// those sections states only this fixture's delta and cites the sibling
// rather than re-deriving them.
//
// # The shape
//
//   CostAssembly
//     sub plate  = Plate()                 — Costed, one free auto
//     sub spacer = Spacer()                — Costed, one free auto (a DIFFERENT structure)
//     minimize cost(self.descendants)      — INLINED aggregate (load-bearing), spans BOTH children
//
// Unlike the single-child `examples/whole_model_joint_drive.ri`, this fixture
// couples TWO DISTINCT Costed children into ONE cluster — a genuinely
// WHOLE-model gate (§6 BT1's shape), not a restatement of that single-child
// boundary test.
//
// `Plate`/`Spacer` each implement the stdlib `Costed` trait
// (crates/reify-compiler/stdlib/io.ri), which supplies the derived cell
//
//     let line_cost : Money = unit_cost * quantity_produced
//
// Neither may re-declare `line_cost` — that derived cell IS the coupling the
// whole seam drives through.  `cost(self.descendants)` expands to
// `[CostAssembly.plate.line_cost, CostAssembly.spacer.line_cost].sum`, so the
// parent's objective reads TWO cells, each a function of its own child's auto.
//
// # Merged vs. frozen — the per-child figures
//
// Each auto is bracketed by a NON-DEGENERATE box, and the two children are
// given DIFFERENT unit_costs and DIFFERENT box widths so neither child's
// contribution is a scaled copy of the other's:
//
//   Plate:  0.0 ≤ quantity_produced ≤ 100.0,  unit_cost = 0.50USD
//   Spacer: 0.0 ≤ quantity_produced ≤  40.0,  unit_cost = 2.25USD
//
// `line_cost = unit_cost × quantity_produced` is strictly increasing in the
// auto over both intervals. Same mechanism as
// `examples/whole_model_joint_drive.ri` (see its "Why the merged figures are
// the SEED, not the exact argmin" section for the full derivation, not
// repeated here): with the `minimize` stripped, FROZEN forms no cluster, so
// each child resolves ALONE at its own synthesised Chebyshev BOX CENTRE;
// MERGED (this file) unions `{CostAssembly, Plate, Spacer}` into ONE cluster
// (dimension 2, far below `WHOLE_MODEL_CLUSTER_DIM_CAP` = 12), no centrality
// objective is synthesised, and cost-minimisation drives BOTH autos toward
// their lower brackets instead — which is why BOTH boxes' LOWER brackets must
// contain the solver's fixed 0.01 seed (same seed-fallback reason as the
// sibling file; a bound above 0.01 reports `RobustnessFloorInfeasible`).
//
//   FROZEN CASCADE (the same model with the parent's `minimize` removed):
//     Plate:  quantity_produced → 50.0  ((0.0+100.0)/2)   line_cost → 25.00 USD
//     Spacer: quantity_produced → 20.0  ((0.0+ 40.0)/2)   line_cost → 45.00 USD
//     Whole-assembly total: 25.00 + 45.00 = 70.00 USD.
//   MERGED (this file, with the `minimize`):
//     Plate:  quantity_produced → 0.01                    line_cost → 0.005  USD
//     Spacer: quantity_produced → 0.01                    line_cost → 0.0225 USD
//     Whole-assembly total: 0.005 + 0.0225 = 0.0275 USD.
//
//   Every figure above is the derivation AND was CONFIRMED OBSERVED verbatim
//   by running both evals (the `mwhole_bt4_*` tests in
//   crates/reify-eval/tests/joint_drive_expansion_boundary.rs read these same
//   cells). The tests assert none of these as absolutes — only the STRICT
//   comparative directions, never an absolute converged value or a tuned
//   tolerance — so this arithmetic is documentation, not a pin.
//
// # Reading the result
//
// A solver-resolved auto is written back STRUCTURE-KEYED (`Plate.quantity_produced`,
// `Spacer.quantity_produced`), which is how the solver keys its `auto_params`;
// the instance-path spelling (`CostAssembly.plate.quantity_produced`, etc.) is
// not written for it in either half.  Read each child's own cells —
// `Plate.quantity_produced`/`Plate.line_cost` and
// `Spacer.quantity_produced`/`Spacer.line_cost` — for the structure-keyed
// story.
//
// # BT3 — the cross-scope surface read
//
// The parent's `minimize cost(self.descendants)` above is ITSELF the
// cross-scope surface read BT3 observes: it expands to
// `[CostAssembly.plate.line_cost, CostAssembly.spacer.line_cost].sum`, and
// each of those two instance-path cells is a function of its child's
// CO-SOLVED `auto` (`line_cost = unit_cost * quantity_produced`), freshly
// refolded in THIS merged solve — not the bottom-up frozen value, and not
// `Undef`.
//
// There is deliberately NO parent-level named `let` here (e.g. a
// `plate_cost_observed : Money = self.plate.line_cost` a design author
// might reach for to give that read a friendly name) — confirmed (esc-5017-7,
// re-verified during this file's own authoring) to be PERMANENTLY `Undef` in
// every half: `build_dependent_cells`'s seed walk starts FROM
// objective/constraint terms only and sweeps their own upstream dependencies
// (`crates/reify-eval/src/engine_eval.rs:1611`), so a purely downstream
// consumer `let` is never swept in, and separately `evaluate_let_bindings`
// runs BEFORE `materialize_dependent_cells` writes the solved cross-scope
// alias back. This is an engine gap owned by β/α
// (docs/prds/v0_6/whole-model-joint-drive-seam.md), not a fixture-authoring
// one — tracked as a follow-up (#5835)
// outside this example's scope.
//
// The raw auto's own instance path (e.g. `CostAssembly.plate.quantity_produced`)
// is likewise deliberately NOT read anywhere in this file, and never will
// resolve: `build_dependent_cells` never emits an instance-path alias that
// would shadow an auto (`!auto_ids.contains(alias)`,
// `crates/reify-eval/src/engine_eval.rs:1854`), and sub-elaboration skips
// autos outright (`unfold.rs:392-395` filters on `ValueCellKind::Param`;
// an `Auto` cell carries no `default_expr` to elaborate).  So that spelling
// is `Undef` by construction — read the auto only via its STRUCTURE-KEYED
// cell (`Plate.quantity_produced`/`Spacer.quantity_produced`), per "Reading
// the result" above.
//
// Integration test:
//   crates/reify-eval/tests/joint_drive_expansion_boundary.rs (`mwhole_bt4_*`,
//   `mwhole_bt3_*`) asserts (i) each child's auto resolves STRICTLY BELOW its
//   frozen-cascade freeze, (ii) the merged whole-assembly cost is STRICTLY
//   LESS than the frozen-cascade baseline — with that baseline derived
//   in-test by evaluating this same model minus the `minimize`, never from a
//   recorded constant — and (iii) a cross-scope surface read of each child's
//   `line_cost` (the objective's own expansion) surfaces the CO-SOLVED
//   value, not a frozen or Undef one.
//
// # TRAP — the aggregate MUST stay inlined in the `minimize`
//
// Same trap as `examples/whole_model_joint_drive.ri`'s "TRAP" section: a `let
// subtree_cost = cost(self.descendants)` + `minimize subtree_cost` forms NO
// cluster (pinned executably by
// `objective_must_inline_the_aggregate_to_couple`,
// `crates/reify-eval/src/resolve_order.rs`) — `examples/cost_subtree_aggregate.ri`
// is exactly that non-coupling shape; do not copy its form here.
//
// # Why auto(free), not strict auto
//
// `docs/prds/v0_6/whole-model-objective-coupling.md` §11 open question 3 left
// this tactical choice to "decide during ε". Same reasoning and precedent as
// `examples/whole_model_joint_drive.ri`'s "Why auto(free)" section: a strict
// `auto` would trigger the uniqueness re-solve, and a `ConstraintNonUnique`
// error would mask the cost signal this example exists to publish.
//
// # One non-collection instance path per structure
//
// `Plate` and `Spacer` are each reachable by EXACTLY ONE non-collection
// instance path (`sub plate = Plate()`, `sub spacer = Spacer()`).  Two subs of
// the SAME structure, or a `List<T>` collection sub, would be DROPPED by
// `build_single_instance_alias_paths` (N runtime paths would share one
// template `default_expr`), killing the instance-path alias BT3 depends on —
// this is why the fixture uses two DISTINCT Costed structures rather than two
// instances of one.
//
// # v1 boundary
//
// Same v1 boundary as `examples/whole_model_joint_drive.ri`: DEPTH-1 Costed
// descendants only (see `examples/cost_subtree_aggregate.ri`), one auto per
// child — well inside the whole-model cluster dimension cap.

structure def Plate : Costed {
    param supplier          : String = "Acme Sheet Metal"
    param part_number       : String = "P-1180"
    param unit_cost         : Money  = 0.50USD
    param lead_time         : Time   = 48h

    // The joint-drive target.  Bracketed by a NON-DEGENERATE box so the
    // cost-minimising direction and the frozen Chebyshev centre (50.0) are far
    // apart — that separation is what makes the coupling observable.  The
    // lower bracket must contain the solver's fixed 0.01 seed for a
    // dimensionless auto; see the header's "Why the merged figures are the
    // SEED" note.
    param quantity_produced : Real   = auto(free)
    constraint quantity_produced >= 0.0
    constraint quantity_produced <= 100.0
}

structure def Spacer : Costed {
    param supplier          : String = "Misumi"
    param part_number       : String = "S-2240"
    param unit_cost         : Money  = 2.25USD
    param lead_time         : Time   = 72h

    // A NARROWER, differently-priced box than Plate's — so the two children's
    // contributions are not a scaled copy of one another and each auto is
    // independently distinguishable in the eval result. Lower bracket still
    // contains the 0.01 seed.
    param quantity_produced : Real   = auto(free)
    constraint quantity_produced >= 0.0
    constraint quantity_produced <= 40.0
}

structure CostAssembly {
    sub plate  = Plate()
    sub spacer = Spacer()

    // INLINED — never behind a `let`.  Spans BOTH children, which is what
    // makes this a WHOLE-model cluster rather than two independent
    // single-child solves.
    //
    // This `minimize` term IS the fixture's only cross-scope surface read —
    // see the header's "BT3 — the cross-scope surface read" section for why
    // NO parent-level `let` (e.g. `let plate_cost_observed = self.plate.
    // line_cost`) is declared here.
    minimize cost(self.descendants)
}
